cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cMeta in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "cMeta (Common Meta Framework)"
abstract: >-
  cMeta (also known as cX) is a small, portable framework for unifying,
  interconnecting and reusing code, data, models, agents and knowledge across
  projects, platforms and time through a single uniform interface, designed for
  collaborative and reproducible research, development and experimentation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fursin
    given-names: Grigori
    website: "https://cTuning.ai/@gfursin"
    affiliation: "cTuning Labs"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7719-1624"
version: "0.32.0"
date-released: "2026-08-02"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cTuningLabs/cmeta"
url: "https://cTuning.ai"
keywords:
  - reproducible research
  - meta-framework
  - content-addressable artifacts
  - machine learning systems
  - benchmarking
  - co-design
  - automation

# Selected prior work by the author describing the concepts behind cMeta and its
# predecessors (Collective Knowledge, Collective Mind / CMX), which this project
# builds upon.
